Started to look into this earlier today. Had hoped it might be a quick thing to knock off, but after digging into it for 15min and talking to @thc202 a bit, here's what we came up with.

* ~ProxiesParamProxy > Should be made public as that provides a simple IP/Host and Port representation of a proxy.~ Done in https://github.com/zaproxy/zaproxy/pull/5785
* Might need to add some sort of proxy utils class (or functionality to an existing class [ExtensionProxies, or ProxiesParamProxy]), to do things like get a list of all ZAPs proxies (primary and alt) [see below], have a proxy.toString() method, comparison checks (equal, 0.0.0.0, loopback, etc):
```java
private List<ProxiesParamProxy> getAllProxies() {
    List<ProxiesParamProxy> proxies = new ArrayList<ProxiesParamProxy>();
    proxies.add(new ProxiesParamProxy(
            Model.getSingleton().getOptionsParam().getProxyParam().getProxyIp(),
            Model.getSingleton().getOptionsParam().getProxyParam().getProxyPort(), true));
    ExtensionProxies ep = Control.getSingleton().getExtensionLoader()
            .getExtension(ExtensionProxies.class);
    proxies.addAll(ep.getAdditionalProxies());
    return proxies;
}
```

* Handling the checks for the API are more straight forward than the GUI, since only one option can be changed at a time.
* Handling the check for the GUI mean that the user could start ZAP, add an alt proxy (or change the primary), then setup a proxy chain before clicking Ok (or the opposite order). In both cases a mechanism is needed whereby we can "know" the current list (from the config and as yet unapplied changes), so:
  - AbstractParamDialog.getBtnOK might need to check that it validates first then it saves the params.
  - We need to check the actual values that are set in the UI at the time of the validation (which are not currently exposed in any way).
  - Maybe we could save the current options to a temp param and pass it in the validate method, that way other panels would see/check wants going to be set in other options
